==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|NL.|-}}, from {{der|en|la|sputum||that which is spit out, spittle}}, from {{m|la|spuere||to spit}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|sputa}}

# {{lb|en|physiology}} Matter coughed up and [[expectorate]]d from the mouth, composed of [[saliva]] and discharges from the respiratory passages such as [[mucus]], [[phlegm]] or [[pus]].
#* {{quote-web|en|author=James Hamblin|work=The Atlantic|date=2020-02-24|title=You’re Likely to Get the Coronavirus|url=https://www.theatlantic.com/health/archive/2020/02/covid-vaccine/607000/|passage=At the U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention in Atlanta, the boy’s '''sputum''' sat for a month, waiting for its turn in a slow process of antibody-matching analysis.}}

